In March 2017, [[Dan Reynolds]] told ''[[People (magazine)|People]]'' that the song was inspired by his experiences with [[ankylosing spondylitis]] that he developed, elaborating by saying:
{{blockquote
|The meaning of the song is really reflecting on specific things in my life that were painful, whether it was anxiety and dealing with crowds, feeling overwhelmed by that or the success of the band, disease, going through depression—anything that was a source of pain in my life. And just rising above that, finding a place of perspective where I could be appreciative of the pain in my life and make it my greatest strength.<ref>{{cite magazine |last=Mizoguchi |first=Karen |url=http://people.com/music/imagine-dragons-dan-reynolds-believer-ankylosing-spondylitis/ |title=How Health Issues Made Imagine Dragons' Dan Reynolds a 'Believer' Again: 'I'm Appreciative of the Pain in My Life' |date=March 9, 2017 |work=[[People (magazine)|People]] |access-date=July 16, 2017 |archive-date=August 5, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200805203349/https://people.com/music/imagine-dragons-dan-reynolds-believer-ankylosing-spondylitis/ |url-status=live }}</ref>
}}

"Believer" was written by Imagine Dragons members [[Dan Reynolds]], [[Wayne Sermon]], [[Ben McKee]], and [[Daniel Platzman]], along with Stephen Robertson, [[Alex da Kid]], and its producers [[Mattman & Robin|Robin Fredriksson and Mattias Larsson]],<ref name="American Songwriter">{{Cite magazine |last=Houghton |first=Cillea |date=November 13, 2023 |title=The Empowering Meaning Behind Imagine Dragons' 'Believer' |url=https://americansongwriter.com/the-empowering-meaning-behind-imagine-dragons-believer/ |access-date=March 4, 2026 |magazine=[[American Songwriter]]}}</ref> around the time of the [[2016 United States presidential election|2016 U.S. presidential election]].<ref name="The Advocate">{{Cite magazine |date=October 18, 2018 |title=Imagine Dragons' Dan Reynolds on Why 'Believer' Is a Queer Anthem |magazine=[[The Advocate (magazine)|The Advocate]] |last=Reynolds |first=Daniel |url=https://www.advocate.com/music/2018/10/18/imagine-dragons-dan-reynolds-why-believer-queer-anthem |access-date=March 4, 2026}}</ref> The song marked the band's first time working with Mattman & Robin and Tranter, of whom Reynolds said helped the band get back on track. He called "Believer" "one of those songs that was waiting to be written", with the song coming quickly while they were in a room with Tranter.<ref name="Grammy">{{Cite web |last=Moayeri |first=Lily |date=August 5, 2022 |title=Inside Imagine Dragons' Biggest Hits: Dan Reynolds Details How 'Believer,' 'Radioactive' & More Came to Be |url=https://www.grammy.com/news/imagine-dragons-songs-stories-believer-radioactive-thunder-enemy-mercury-act-1-2-new-album-2022-dan-reynolds-interview |access-date=March 4, 2026 |website=[[Grammy Awards]]}}</ref>

It was released on February 1, 2017, under [[Kidinakorner]] and [[Interscope Records]],<ref name=iTunes>{{cite web|url=https://itunes.apple.com/us/album/believer-single/id1200626096|title=Believer - Single by Imagine Dragons on Apple Music|website=[[iTunes Store]] (US)|access-date=May 15, 2017|archive-date=February 2, 2017|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170202122458/https://itunes.apple.com/us/album/believer-single/id1200626096|url-status=dead}}</ref> as the lead single to the band's third studio album, ''[[Evolve (Imagine Dragons album)|Evolve]]'' (2017).<ref>{{Cite web |title=Imagine Dragons' 'Evolve' Debuts at No. 1 on Top Rock & Alternative Albums Charts |url=https://www.billboard.com/pro/imagine-dragons-evolve-no-1-top-rock-alternative-chart/ |last=Rutherford |first=Kevin |date=July 6, 2017 |access-date=January 7, 2026 |website=[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]}}</ref>

